-- BASELINE SCHEMA — THE ONE MIGRATION A FRESH DATABASE NEEDS
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Generated by pg_dump --schema-only from the live schema on 2026-08-16 and
-- verified by restoring it into an empty database with zero errors. It creates
-- 109 tables, 269 RLS policies, 21 functions, 39 triggers, 18 enums, 160
-- foreign keys and 184 indexes.
--
-- ── WHY THE PREVIOUS 99 MIGRATIONS WERE ARCHIVED ───────────────────────────
--
-- They could not rebuild the database. Three independent reasons, each fatal:
--
--   1. ORDERING. `scheduled_emails` is ALTERed in 20251014163527 and not
--      CREATEd until 20260426053659 — seven months later. `supabase db push`
--      into an empty database fails there, and did.
--
--   2. MISSING OBJECTS. Seven tables have no CREATE statement in any migration:
--      agent_presence, call_attempts, dialer_campaigns, dialer_locks,
--      dialer_sessions, lead_imports, telnyx_events. They were created through
--      the dashboard and the repo never learned about them.
--
--   3. THE OLD BASELINE WAS INCOMPLETE BY ITS OWN ADMISSION. It captured 83
--      CREATE TABLEs and explicitly not foreign keys, indexes, RLS policies,
--      triggers or enums. Restoring from it would have produced tables with
--      NONE of the 269 policies — every row readable by any authenticated user.
--
-- The archived files remain in supabase/migrations-archive/ and in git history.
-- They are a record of how the schema got here; this file is what reproduces it.
--
-- ── ADDING TO THIS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- Write new migrations normally, after this one. Do NOT edit this file to add a
-- column — that is what makes a baseline rot back into an unreplayable chain.
-- Regenerate it only when squashing again, and re-verify by restoring into an
-- empty database.
